{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4f3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a91f-5a05-7370-bf74-ffa98261cad4"},"sequence":212,"recorded_at":1780531400000419,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d48d36b9-6599-476a-89c2-ba7d2fcc06eb","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"d48d36b9-6599-476a-89c2-ba7d2fcc06eb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d48d36b9-6599-476a-89c2-ba7d2fcc06eb"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a91f-e562-7b41-a112-3cb766234025"},"task_id":"01a0a91f-e562-7b41-a112-3cb766234025","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a91f-e562-7b41-a112-3cb766234025","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/outputs/RunnerControl/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260916-13diw4/TASK-260916-13diw4_outcome_v6.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-13diw4: register-mac-and-repository-access — developer outcome v6\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review`, uncommitted candidate in story worktree).\n4|\n5|Focused R6 delivery per `revision6-canonical-lease.md` and `revision6-recovery-FIRST.md`:\n6|fixes R5-F1 (`changes_requested`, `repeat-of: revision 4 / R4-F1`) — the directory\n7|lease could be bypassed through a symlink alias — and recovers the cancelled\n8|RUN-260916-0e9d43 validation, whose preserved source edits are completed here.\n9|Prior M1–M29 regions were not rerun per contract (unchanged code); the M9\n10|survivor bound is restated from v3/v5.\n11|\n12|## Fixes (code)\n13|\n14|Preserved from the cancelled run (verified, not rewritten): canonical `leaseKey`\n15|via nearest-existing-ancestor symlink resolution, original-key hold across\n16|awaits with exact-key release, `ensureNoAlias` refusal before side effects, and\n17|the three R6 tests. This run adds two surgical corrections:\n18|\n19|1. **`ensureNoAlias` no longer conflates symlinks with Finder aliases.**\n20|   `URLResourceValues.isAliasFileKey` is also true for symlinks such as the\n21|   system `/var` and `/tmp` links that every temporary path resolves through,\n22|   so the preserved check refused ALL installs under temp roots with\n23|   `invalidDraft(\"... resolves through a Finder alias at '/var'\")`. Fix:\n24|   skip components where `destinationOfSymbolicLink` succeeds (symlinks are\n25|   canonicalized by `leaseKey`, not refused); only non-symlink aliases throw.\n26|   This was also the root cause of the validation hang: the refused download\n27|   left `installPath` nil, the register step failed with \"Install the runner\n28|   package first\", `config.sh` never started, and `waitStarted()` suspended\n29|   forever while the testing helper outlived its parent.\n30|2. **Bounded latch wait in `reviewerSymlinkAliasCannotBypassDirectoryLease`.**\n31|   New `waitForConfigStart(_:timeoutSeconds:)` (30 s poll of the latch flag,\n32|   no leaked continuations) plus a pre-latch gate check that fails fast with\n33|   the recorded Flow failure. A config that never starts is now a reported\n34|   failure with diagnostics, never a hang. Regression steps, transport queue,\n35|   and both `#expect` assertions are otherwise identical to the attached rev5\n36|   attack source; semantics preserved, not weakened.\n37|\n38|## AC coverage — 8 of 8 rows driven through production entry points\n39|\n40|| # | AC row | Named committed test(s) | Production call site |\n41||---|--------|-------------------------|----------------------|\n42|| 1 | Org registration without terminal | `orgWizardEndToEndDeletesTokenAndLeaksNothing`, `reviewerInFlightInstallCannotRepopulateChangedDraft`, `reviewerRetryCannotRunTwoConfigsInSameDirectory`, `cancelDuringConfigKeepsLeaseAndRecoversAfterSettle`, `reviewerSymlinkAliasCannotBypassDirectoryLease` | `Flow.apply` (.beginDraft/.resolveGroup/.downloadAndInstall/.registerRunner/.setupService/.retry/.cancel) |\n43|| 2 | Repo registration without terminal | `repoWizardOmitsRunnerGroup`, `repoRunnerListRequestUsesQueryNotEncodedPath` | same Flow effects; no `runner-groups` traffic, no `--runnergroup` argv |\n44|| 3 | Selected repos are applied | `orgResolveGroupCreatesWithSelectedRepos`, `repoAccessAppliesAndConfirmsRealIDs`, `repositoryConfirmationFollowsPagination`, `inFlightAccessAbandonedWhenRepositoriesEdited` | `createGroup` / `setGroupRepositories` + paginated `fetchGroupRepositories` confirm |\n45|| 4 | Repo access and labels changeable | `repoAccessAppliesAndConfirmsRealIDs`, `labelsApplyRequiresRealRunnerIDThenPuts`, `inFlightLabelsAbandonedWhenLabelsEdited` | `Flow.apply(.applyRepositoryAccess/.applyLabels)` with verified IDs |\n46|| 5 | Failed ops avoid orphans | `failedConfigDeletesTokenAndReportsScrubbedError`, `registerIsIdempotentAcrossRetries`, `registerRefusesMismatchedRemoteIdentity`, `cancelDuringConfigKeepsLeaseAndRecoversAfterSettle` (both tokens deleted) | `Flow.registerRunner` (token deleted on every failure path; single mint/config) |\n47|| 6 | Repeated ops avoid duplicates | `registerIsIdempotentAcrossRetries`, `retryResumesFailedDownloadWithoutDuplicates`, `remoteDuplicateWithoutReplaceIsRefusedBeforeToken`, `runnerListFollowsPaginationForDuplicateGuard`, `existingRegistrationBlocksFreshInstall`, `reviewerRetryCannotRunTwoConfigsInSameDirectory` (1 config call), `beginDraftDuringDownloadKeepsDirectoryLease`, `resetDuringDownloadKeepsDirectoryLeaseUntilSettled`, `nonconflictingInstallProceedsWhileOtherDirectoryRuns` (scope control), `reviewerSymlinkAliasCannotBypassDirectoryLease` (alias spelling, 1 config call) | complete-list `rejectRemoteDuplicate` gate + installer markers + canonical directory lease + owner lock |\n48|| 7 | No secret leakage | `orgWizardEndToEndDeletesTokenAndLeaksNothing`, `runConfigScrubsTokenFromFailure`, `failedConfigDeletesTokenAndReportsScrubbedError`, `cancelDuringConfigKeepsLeaseAndRecoversAfterSettle` | token only in config.sh argv in memory; absent from actions/URLs/headers/bodies; deleted after use |\n49|| 8 | Tests exercise actual entry points | all Flow tests + `setupServiceWritesManualPlistFoundByDiscovery`, `runConfigExecutesRealScript`, `staleRegisterFailureDoesNotUnlockOrPlantFailure`, `scopeChangeClearsCompletedStepsInState`, `leaseKeyCanonicalizesSymlinkAncestorsForMissingLeaf`, `finderAliasInstallFolderIsRefusedBeforeDownload` | `Flow.apply`, `RunnerInstallerService.*`, `State.reduce`, cross-checked by `RunnerDiscovery.installed` and a real shell `config.sh` |\n50|\n51|Negative/refusal coverage: all v3/v4/v5 negatives retained and green, plus the\n52|adopted rev5 alias attack and the R6 ancestor/alias controls.\n53|\n54|## Narrowing-mutant evidence\n55|\n56|Changed gate only (M1–M29 unchanged regions not rerun per contract):\n57|\n58|| Mutant | Admits exactly | Named failing test(s) | Result |\n59||--------|----------------|-----------------------|--------|\n60|| M30: `leaseKey` reduced to spelling-only `standardizedFileURL.path` (no symlink resolution), fixed `ensureNoAlias` kept | symlink-alias spellings only | `reviewerSymlinkAliasCannotBypassDirectoryLease` (2 issues: 2 config calls; attested-complete vs .runner mismatch — the exact R5-F1 signature) | KILLED, exit 1; control `reviewerRetryCannotRunTwoConfigsInSameDirectory` (same-spelling class) passes exit 0 under the mutant |\n61|| M30 revert | — | pristine sha256 `ecc84edc…59cc4a` verified after revert; alias test re-run green | REVERTED |\n62|\n63|No survivors in M30. Prior M9 (`createGroup` default true→false) survivor bound\n64|restated from v3 (unchanged code, not rerun): the default is not load-bearing,\n65|Flow passes `true` explicitly, M9b kills the call site.\n66|\n67|The source-text-token mutant rule does not apply: no gate inspects source text.\n68|\n69|## Verification commands (real exit codes)\n70|\n71|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` (CI gate):\n72|  **exit 0, 157 tests passed** (154 + 3 R6), full log at `/tmp/r6_full.log`.\n73|- Focused lifecycle filter (R6 trio + 7 R5 controls + `downloadRefusesMissingChecksum`):\n74|  **exit 0, 11 tests passed**.\n75|- M30 mutant runs: alias test **exit 1** (2 issues, killed); same-spelling\n76|  control **exit 0**; revert sha256 match confirmed.\n77|- `python3 -m unittest discover -s Scripts/tests` (CI gate): **exit 0, 4 tests OK**.\n78|- `xcodebuild -workspace RunnerControl.xcworkspace -scheme RunnerControl\n79|  -destination 'platform=macOS' build`: **BUILD SUCCEEDED** (exit 0, 7.8 s).\n80|- No repo-configured lint gate (CI `ci.yml` runs only the two test jobs above;\n81|  no `.swiftlint.yml`/`.swiftformat`).\n82|- Hang bisection evidence: pure `leaseKey` control and Finder-alias control\n83|  passed while fixture tests failed naming `/var` as an alias; trivial-filter\n84|  run green — isolating the hang to the test's unbounded latch wait behind a\n85|  gate error, fixed as described above.\n86|- Generator inputs untouched: `ios-app-manager.json`, `Project.swift`,\n87|  `Workspace.swift`, `Package.swift` unmodified (this run edited only the two\n88|  existing candidate files); existing production runners untouched (all test IO\n89|  under temp roots; services never bootstrapped); candidate left UNCOMMITTED,\n90|  no producer commit (branch tip still `6b4a21d`).\n91|\n92|## Files changed (all UNCOMMITTED in story worktree, as required)\n93|\n94|- `Packages/RunnerControlCore/Sources/RunnerInstallerService.swift` —\n95|  canonical `leaseKey` (nearest-existing-ancestor resolution, original-key\n96|  hold/release), `ensureNoAlias` with symlink exclusion.\n97|- `Packages/RunnerControlCore/Tests/RunnerRegistrationTests.swift` —\n98|  adopted `reviewerSymlinkAliasCannotBypassDirectoryLease` with bounded\n99|  `waitForConfigStart` + pre-latch gate check,\n100|  `leaseKeyCanonicalizesSymlinkAncestorsForMissingLeaf`,\n101|  `finderAliasInstallFolderIsRefusedBeforeDownload`, `DownloadCounter`.\n102|\n103|## Stated bounds (unknowns, not guesses)\n104|\n105|- Live registration smoke remains a separate delivery task; transport covered\n106|  by fakes, filesystem by temp-root fixtures with real `tar`/`shasum`/`config.sh`.\n107|- Authenticated download `sha256_checksum` availability was confirmed\n108|  nonempty for osx x64/arm64 by root read-only live API (per revision-4\n109|  contract); this run made no live GitHub calls.\n110|- Pagination cap is 100 pages per list (fail-closed throw, never silent partial).\n111|- Mid-step session change is bound by single-auth reuse (no mixing); an\n112|  inter-step change invalidates via `syncServerBinding` plus `.runner`/marker\n113|  verification.\n114|- Ownership table stays per-Mac (`~/Library/GitHubActions/\n115|  .runnercontrol-groups.json`); two local users do not share it.\n116|- A same-directory retry refused with `directoryBusy` mints and deletes a\n117|  short-lived registration token for the register step before reaching the\n118|  lease; the token is never used for a second config and never retained.\n119|- Alias refusal covers alias components in the given installation spelling;\n120|  a symlink that resolves to a target containing an alias elsewhere is\n121|  canonicalized by `leaseKey`, not refused as an alias.","final_result":true}}}
