{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf99","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a91f-5a05-7370-bf74-ffa98261cad4"},"sequence":1575,"recorded_at":1780531400003145,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"d48d36b9-6599-476a-89c2-ba7d2fcc06eb","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"d48d36b9-6599-476a-89c2-ba7d2fcc06eb","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"d48d36b9-6599-476a-89c2-ba7d2fcc06eb"},"terminal":"completed","text":"R7 work is ready for review (board `to-review`, handoff accepted, checklist 19/19).\n\nWhat changed: the canonical directory lease in `RunnerInstallerService.swift` now folds case via POSIX lowercasing when the real volume reports case-insensitive names, so `macbook-test` and `MACBOOK-TEST` share one lease while the leaf is still absent. Sensitivity is queried per volume, never assumed; unknown volumes fail closed toward folding. Original-key hold/release and download/config/service/recovery identity are unchanged.\n\nTests: adopted the rev6 case-alias regression through `Flow.apply` with one documented correction — the inode proof runs after the original settles, since the attached order (leaf absent, then inode present, with only a refused operation between) is unsatisfiable on any correct fix. Added a forced-sensitive Flow control proving distinct leases are preserved, and a folding/stability unit control. New tests: 3, all passing.\n\nEvidence: full Core suite exit 0 with 160/160 passing and 0 issues, metadata tests exit 0 (4 OK), native build succeeded. Narrowing mutant M31 (folding disabled) is killed by the adopted regression with exit 1 and the exact rev6 4-issue signature, while same-spelling, symlink, and ancestor controls stay green under the mutant; pristine hash verified after revert. AC coverage is 8 of 8 rows driven, reported in the attached `TASK-260916-13diw4_outcome_v7.md`. Candidate left uncommitted, generator inputs untouched, no production runner touched.","reason":null}}
